@startuml
title TplQueue Blazor sample — current source and integration boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "TplQueue.Usage — sample source projects" {
  component "TplQueue.Sample.BlazorSignalR\nnet8.0\nHost / composition\nSnapshot capture / bounded retention" as Host
  component "TplQueue.Sample.Domain\nnetstandard2.0\nJob / graph factories, payloads, handlers\nBusiness store, queue / cache wrappers" as Domain
  component "TplQueue.Sample.Etl.Contracts\nnetstandard2.0\nShared sample interfaces and DTOs" as Contracts
  component "TplQueue.Sample.Simulation\nnetstandard2.0\nWorkflows / scheduled admission\nSession, queue runtime, graph catalog" as Simulation
}

package "External packages — direct references only" {
  component "Fmacias.TplQueue.Core" as Core
  component "Fmacias.TplQueue.Microsoft.DependencyInjection" as DI
  component "Fmacias.TplQueue.Cache.MemCache" as MemCache
  component "Fmacias.TplQueue.Abstractions" as Abstractions
  component "Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions\n9.0.8" as MsDI
  component "Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions\n9.0.8" as MsLog
}

component "tools/TplQueue.JobMonitor\nMaintained Web Component / JS bridge assets" as Assets
component "Browser\njob-queue-timeline\nPer-view selection / time / viewport" as Browser

Host --> Domain : ProjectReference
Host --> Contracts : ProjectReference
Host --> Simulation : ProjectReference
Domain --> Contracts : ProjectReference
Simulation --> Contracts : ProjectReference

Host --> Core : PackageReference
Host --> DI : PackageReference
Domain --> MemCache : PackageReference
Contracts --> Abstractions : PackageReference
Simulation --> MsDI : PackageReference
Simulation --> MsLog : PackageReference

Host ..> Simulation : Subscribe observer, then Start\nStopAsync on host shutdown / user stop
Simulation ..> Domain : DI implementations via Contracts\nISampleJobFactory and queue wrappers
Simulation ..> Host : IJobEvent from runtime-owned queues\nMembership via ISimulationGraphCatalog
Assets ..> Host : MSBuild synchronizes assets\ninto ignored wwwroot/job-monitor
Host ..> Browser : Blazor Interactive Server circuit\nJobEventSnapshot window + queue/membership metadata
Browser ..> Host : Selection callback / Stop arrivals control

note bottom of Simulation
  One System.Threading.Timer per ScheduledWorkflow.
  Singleton IEtlQueueRuntime holds the actual queues.
  Simulation has no Domain ProjectReference.
  Stop/Completion concern delivery, not job drain.
end note

note bottom of Contracts
  Shared beyond ETL: factory, queue runtime,
  workflow/session, graph membership and DTOs.
  Proposed future name: TplQueue.Sample.Contracts.
  No rename has been applied.
end note

note bottom of Browser
  Initial retained window, then observer-driven updates.
  event-stream.js derives current renderer positions.
  No custom application hub, REST API or polling.
  Browsers do not start or own workloads.
end note

legend bottom
  Solid arrows: direct .csproj references.
  Dotted arrows: runtime calls/data or asset integration.
  TplQueue package versions use TplQueuePackageVersion
  (Directory.Build.props; current default 0.2.0-preview.2).
  Transitive package references and private product internals
  are intentionally outside this diagram.
endlegend
@enduml
